<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover"><meta name="description" content="A consequential water shift with paid work and first-hand reports."><link rel="icon" href="data:,"><title>Across the cut · Human Framework</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/web/across.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/web/game-shell.css"></head>
<body class="compact-game" data-game="across"><div class="shell"><header><a href="/games/">← Games</a><span>TWO STATIONS · ONE LAUNCH</span></header><main>
<section class="game-hud"><div class="hud-top"><h1>Across the cut</h1><div class="hud-clock"><strong id="minute">0</strong><span>of 30 shift minutes</span></div></div><p class="hud-objective">Two water units for the launch. You operate the valve; Deniz handles the inlet.</p><p id="resources" class="hud-resources"></p><div class="hud-bodies"><span id="location"></span><span id="condition"></span></div><p id="latest-alert" class="hud-alert" role="status"></p><p id="save-warning" class="save-warning" hidden></p></section>
<p id="notice" role="alert" hidden></p>
<nav class="game-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Shift views"><button id="tab-work" class="game-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="panel-work">Work</button><button id="tab-notebook" class="game-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-notebook" tabindex="-1">Notebook</button><button id="tab-brief" class="game-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-brief" tabindex="-1">Brief</button><button id="tab-save" class="game-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-save" tabindex="-1">Save</button></nav>
<div class="game-content">
<section id="panel-work" class="game-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-work" tabindex="0"><div class="panel-heading"><h2 id="work-heading">Your valve</h2><span id="repair-status"></span></div><p id="work-context" class="short-note"></p><div id="work-choices" class="choice-list"></div><details><summary>Move or eat</summary><div id="other-choices" class="choice-list"></div></details><details><summary>Water and stopping</summary><p>Releasing reserves your two units for two paid minutes. Stop before completion to keep them. Once released, water takes three more minutes to reach the launch through the inlet. Deniz must have repaired the inlet and be holding it open when the water arrives.</p><p>Stopping repair keeps every paid minute and the installed fitting. Available time lets you recover automatically; eating uses your owned portion only after two paid minutes.</p></details></section>
<section id="panel-notebook" class="game-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-notebook" tabindex="0" hidden><h2>What you know</h2><p class="short-note">Reports describe what someone observed then. They do not show the other station now.</p><div id="incoming-reports"></div><details open><summary>Latest known facts</summary><ul id="known-facts" class="facts"></ul></details><details><summary>Share your first-hand observations</summary><p class="short-note">Select facts you observed yourself. A message takes one paid minute. Radio uses one charge; contact needs Deniz at your station for the full minute.</p><fieldset id="report-selection"><legend>Your observations</legend></fieldset><div class="buttons"><button id="send-radio">Send by radio · 1 min</button><button id="send-contact">Tell Deniz · 1 min</button></div><p id="radio-note" class="short-note"></p></details><details><summary>Earlier observations and outgoing reports</summary><ol id="observation-history" class="facts"></ol><ol id="sent-reports" class="facts"></ol></details></section>
<section id="panel-brief" class="game-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-brief" tabindex="0" hidden><section id="shift-brief"><h2>Water across the cut</h2><svg class="route-map" viewBox="0 0 640 130" aria-label="Valve, six walking minutes to the inlet, then five cart minutes to the launch" role="img"><path d="M70 55H570"/><circle cx="70" cy="55" r="12"/><circle cx="340" cy="55" r="12"/><path d="M552 46h40l-8 20h-23z"/><text x="70" y="100">Valve · you</text><text x="340" y="100">Inlet</text><text x="570" y="100">Launch</text><text x="205" y="34">6 min walk</text><text x="455" y="34">5 min cart</text></svg><p>You and Deniz serve the same two-unit launch. You own two units at the valve; Deniz owns one cart unit. Pipe water needs both repaired stations and Deniz attending the inlet. The cart reaches the launch after five minutes and then takes five minutes back.</p><p>Inspect to learn your local repair. The launch notice is at the inlet. A delivery at its departure minute still counts.</p><details><summary>How Deniz chooses</summary><p id="receiver-policy"></p></details><details><summary>Time and radio</summary><p id="channel-brief"></p><p>Continue advances to your next useful local event. A received report stops time for your decision while leaving any unfinished job underway. Stop work explicitly if you change your mind. Reading tabs never advances the shift.</p><p>Your shift lasts 30 minutes even if the launch leaves earlier. An unheard event at the other station cannot end your account.</p></details></section><section id="your-account" hidden><h2>Your account</h2><p id="account-summary"></p><ul id="paid-account" class="facts"></ul><p class="short-note">This account uses your own actions and received observations.</p><button id="reveal-outcome">Reveal episode outcome</button><section id="world-outcome" hidden><h3>Researcher view · actual episode outcome</h3><p id="world-summary"></p><ol id="world-timeline" class="facts"></ol></section></section></section>
<section id="panel-save" class="game-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-save" tabindex="0" hidden><h2>Keep your shift</h2><p id="save-status"></p><div class="buttons"><button id="download">Download this shift</button><label class="file-button">Import a saved shift<input id="import" type="file" accept="application/json,.json"></label></div><p class="short-note">One active shift is kept on this device. An imported shift replaces it after your review.</p><button id="download-backup" hidden>Download unreadable device save</button><section id="import-preview" hidden aria-labelledby="import-title"><h3 id="import-title" tabindex="-1">Replace this shift?</h3><p id="import-detail"></p><p class="short-note">Download the current shift first if you want to keep a copy.</p><div class="buttons"><button id="confirm-import">Replace active shift</button><button id="cancel-import">Cancel</button></div></section><details><summary>Start a new shift</summary><p>A new shift replaces this one. Local repair and launch conditions may differ; you learn them through inspection and reports.</p><button id="new-shift">Replace with a new shift</button></details><details class="model-notes"><summary>Model notes</summary><p>This is an authored deterministic game using Human/runtime 0.1.1. Work, capacity, body estimates, information access and Deniz’s policy are software rules, not calibrated measurements of people. There is no LLM, moral-worth score or religious evaluator. Radio reception is automatic; it is not an attention or memory model.</p><p>Save files contain the complete shift recipe, including starting conditions. Ordinary play shows only your character’s information. Downloads can reveal facts that have not yet reached your character.</p></details></section>
</div><section class="game-dock" aria-label="Your work and time controls"><div class="hud-jobs"><div class="hud-job"><strong id="job-label"></strong><span id="job-timing"></span></div></div><div class="game-time-controls"><div class="time-controls"><button id="next-event" class="primary">Continue →</button><button id="one-minute">+1 min</button><button id="stop" hidden>Stop work</button></div><p id="time-status" role="status"></p></div></section>
</main></div><script type="module" src="/web/across-player.js"></script></body></html>
